WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:07.360
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am going to&nbsp;
explain an episode called “The Many Place” from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:15.920
the anthology horror television series “Creeped&nbsp;
Out.” Spoilers ahead! Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:24.640
The Blolesens family has come to North Queensland,&nbsp;
Australia to enjoy their summer vacation. They are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:30.880
staying at a 5 star hotel called Ashgrove.&nbsp;
However, they are welcomed by heavy rainfall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:34.960
because of the place’s tropical climate. As&nbsp;
the parents complain about the weather, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:39.600
receptionist tells them about all the different&nbsp;
activities they can do in the hotel without having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:45.920
to go outdoors. The eldest daughter of the family,&nbsp;
Nita locks eyes with a teenage boy in the lobby.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:50.880
They exchange numbers and decide to meet at the&nbsp;
swimming pool later. The youngest of the family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:56.160
Max runs inside the elevator and presses all the&nbsp;
buttons just for the fun of it. She is stopped by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:01.680
the hotel’s boiler man. He has worked in the hotel&nbsp;
for several years and knows all its secrets. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:07.280
man warns Max against pressing all the buttons,&nbsp;
claiming that bad things happen to kids who do so.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:12.640
He also mentions someone named Qinkin but before&nbsp;
he can elaborate, the hotel clerk approaches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:18.400
them. She reminds him that the elevator is only&nbsp;
for guests and he isn’t allowed to use it.
&nbsp;

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:23.760
The boiler man curses her and walks away,&nbsp;
leaving Max speechless after the encounter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:28.800
The clerk uses her keys to reset the buttons on&nbsp;
the elevator and brings the family to their room.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:34.160
They are staying in a single room, hence the kids&nbsp;
fight about who gets to use the bathroom first.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:39.680
Nita accidentally scrapes Max’s favorite black&nbsp;
sandals in the process. The sisters used to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:44.880
best friends but now that Nita is growing into&nbsp;
a teenager, they have grown apart. Max asks her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.600
father if she will also grow up to become like&nbsp;
her sister. The father understands that she is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:54.800
hurt by Nita’s behavior and consoles her. The&nbsp;
parents want some time free from the children so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:59.360
they send them off to the hotel’s pool. Nita had&nbsp;
planned to meet the guy from earlier and doesn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:04.320
want to take her siblings. But at her parents’&nbsp;
request, she reluctantly brings them along. 
&nbsp;

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:09.360
The middle child, Jett, loves to play video games.&nbsp;
He walks through the hallways while wearing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:14.960
Virtual reality headset and accidentally bumps&nbsp;
into a table, dropping a framed picture. He puts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:20.640
it back upside down before entering the elevator&nbsp;
with his sisters. As usual, Max presses all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:25.760
buttons in the elevator, saying that the lights&nbsp;
look pretty. This time, they do not have a key to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:31.600
reset it. All of a sudden, the elevator shakes&nbsp;
aggressively and starts moving. When it stops,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:37.520
Nita tries to press other buttons but none of them&nbsp;
work. They blame Max for being careless and decide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:42.400
to take the stairs. The hallways look different&nbsp;
to them but the kids do not think much of it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:47.680
Jett also notices that the floor feels cold,&nbsp;
in contrast to how it was some moments ago.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:52.400
They go around the hallways looking for stairs&nbsp;
but cannot find any. The elevator that they came&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:57.920
through is lost and they have no way to return&nbsp;
to their parents. Even the rooms have no numbers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:03.120
which Max thinks is weird. Nita tries calling&nbsp;
her parents but her phone has no signal.
&nbsp;

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:09.520
They knock on one of the doors to ask for help and&nbsp;
see that it is already open. Inside the door lies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:15.040
another hallway that is identical to the one they&nbsp;
are in right now. They check other doors and find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:20.560
out that they are stuck in a maze-like place where&nbsp;
every door leads to a different identical hallway.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:25.360
The younger siblings start to panic but Nita&nbsp;
calms them down. She claims that all they have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:30.640
to do is find the elevator again and return&nbsp;
to their parents. Suddenly, they hear a loud&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:35.360
growl from behind a door. Max claims that&nbsp;
the noise is coming from Quinkin who the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:41.120
boiler man warned her about. As the growling gets&nbsp;
louder, she starts to panic and hyperventilates.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:46.240
Nita asks her to breathe and plays their&nbsp;
favorite bo-bo-ski game to calm her down. 
&nbsp;

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:51.840
But trouble arises when they hear a faint snarling&nbsp;
getting closer. On looking under a door, they see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:57.600
a pair of monsters’ feet on the other side. They&nbsp;
screech in fear and run away through random doors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:02.560
getting further away from their original elevator&nbsp;
in the process. Max runs faster than the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:08.560
two and gets lost. Nita and Jatt try calling her&nbsp;
but she has run down several hallways and cannot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:14.160
hear them. When Matt stops running, she calls for&nbsp;
her siblings and realizes that she has lost them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:20.240
While looking for her, Jett and Nita hear an&nbsp;
elevator door ding followed by melodic music. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:25.520
follow the sound and finally reach the elevator.&nbsp;
Nita doesn’t want to leave without Max but Jett&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:28.960
claims that if they inform their parents,&nbsp;
they will find her quicker. They get on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:34.800
elevator and Jett notices the red interior when he&nbsp;
clearly remembers it being a neutral color before.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:39.280
The elevator shakes as it did earlier, making&nbsp;
them think that they will end up back in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:44.960
maze. However, this time, they reach back to their&nbsp;
floor in the hotel. When they pass the hallway,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:49.440
we notice that the framed picture that was&nbsp;
upside down earlier is now in its correct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:55.200
position. Nita uses the keys to open the door to&nbsp;
their room. However, they are met with a surprise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.200 --> 00:05:00.080
when they see two strangers inside. When asked&nbsp;
what they are doing there, the strangers claim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:04.080
that they have been in the room for a week.
The kids then go to the reception and inquire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:09.040
about their parents. The clerk who checked them&nbsp;
in only a few hours ago claims that no one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:14.160
names are staying at the hotel. The boiler man&nbsp;
overhears their conversation and seems to know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:19.600
the truth about the maze. Back in the hallways,&nbsp;
Max is trying to look for her siblings. She hears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:25.920
a roar and curls up on the floor crying in fear.&nbsp;
Suddenly, someone runs towards her. On looking at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:31.920
the person’s face, Max freezes in shock. Somewhere&nbsp;
else, Nita and Jett are confused out of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:36.960
minds. Nita googles her mother’s name and finds&nbsp;
out her number. The mother picks up the call from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:41.840
her workplace in the other part of the world. When&nbsp;
Nita tries to explain what happened, she stops&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:47.040
her and asks her who she is. It turns out that&nbsp;
the mother is living an entirely different life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:51.840
and has a boyfriend who is not their father.&nbsp;
She insists that she isn’t married and has no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:56.720
kids, and cuts the phone call. The siblings are&nbsp;
left speechless at their mother’s indifference.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.720 --> 00:06:01.520
As they brainstorm ideas to get out of the&nbsp;
situation, the boiler man approaches them.
&nbsp;

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:06.480
He asks them if they pressed all the buttons in&nbsp;
the elevator and calls them out for being idiots.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:11.680
He also explains that the hallway they reach after&nbsp;
pressing the buttons is called the Many Place. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:17.040
is a cluster of pathways to alternate universes,&nbsp;
a place where all the realities meet. When the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:22.320
kids look at him in confusion, he further explains&nbsp;
that their universe is one of many universes that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:27.920
exist in space. Each universe gives birth to the&nbsp;
same people but with different realities. Like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:33.120
their mother who is married and has children in&nbsp;
one reality, is a working woman with a boyfriend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:38.160
in another. The Many Place looks like a maze&nbsp;
at first glance but the doors aren’t as random&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:43.520
as they seem. Each door leads them closer to an&nbsp;
elevator that is the path to an alternate reality.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:49.200
There are a billion of them and hence, to find&nbsp;
the one they came from will need a lot of work.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:53.600
He suggests they retrace their steps through&nbsp;
the doors and find the original elevator that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:59.120
they came from. At last, he also warns them that&nbsp;
looking for the original elevator is not that easy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:03.360
as he has never met someone who found&nbsp;
their way back after getting lost.
&nbsp;

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:08.480
Jett looks outside the window and sees flying&nbsp;
cars that are considered usual in this reality.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:12.320
The brother and sister go back to the&nbsp;
elevator when the boiler man stops them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:16.720
He adds that the Many Place was built as a&nbsp;
way to punish the humans who have committed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:22.800
unfathomable crimes. The place they are going to&nbsp;
has a cruel creature who eats the lost people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:27.920
Hence, the children should be careful if they&nbsp;
want to safely reach their original elevator.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:32.400
Following the encounter, they press all the&nbsp;
buttons and end up back in the Many Place.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:37.520
After looking around for more than an hour, they&nbsp;
finally find another lift. However, on reaching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:42.960
the hotel, they immediately find out that they are&nbsp;
not in their original reality. The place is filled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:48.160
with smoke and the sound of missiles launching can&nbsp;
be heard from outside. It is clear that in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:53.760
reality, the world is at war. They return to the&nbsp;
Many place and start looking for another elevator.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:58.400
After a few more hours they finally find another&nbsp;
one but it is filled with water, denoting that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:02.880
the world is underwater in that reality. 
On their third elevator ride, they reach an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:08.560
abandoned hotel and lose hope of finding their&nbsp;
original reality. Nita breaks down crying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:13.520
realizing that she will never meet her parents&nbsp;
and her sister. When Jett tries to comfort her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:18.560
she tells him that they cannot go down billions&nbsp;
of different elevators. Jett, on the other hand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:23.600
asks her to get it together because she is&nbsp;
supposed to be an adult. With renewed motivation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:28.240
they collect things they might need to navigate&nbsp;
through the maze. They decide that finding Max&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:33.040
is more important than finding their original&nbsp;
reality because she might be scared and lonely.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:38.080
Nita gets a horn, some pencils, and a stick&nbsp;
to fight the creature they had seen earlier.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:42.560
Following that, they enter the Many place and&nbsp;
mark all the doors that they walk through.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:46.960
They call Max using the horn and quickly&nbsp;
cross many hallways. But even after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:51.840
hours of searching, they do not find her. 
All of a sudden, they hear Max’s voice calling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:56.640
them. She is just around the corner but she asks&nbsp;
them to not come near her. When the siblings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.640 --> 00:09:01.920
throw several questions at her, she asks them to&nbsp;
just trust her. She also urges them to keep their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:07.360
eyes closed at all costs because she has someone&nbsp;
else with her who is helping her navigate. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:12.400
they are finally face to face, Max reveals that&nbsp;
the creature behind her is Quinkin, the monster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:17.760
that Boiler had warned them about. Quinkin cannot&nbsp;
help but eat the eyes of people who look at him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:22.080
hence they should keep their eyes closed.&nbsp;
Apart from that, he is a gentle creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:26.960
who has lived in Many place his entire life.&nbsp;
He knows every corner of the place and wants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:31.600
to help them get back to their original reality.&nbsp;
Max and Nita hug while still keeping their eyes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:36.720
closed. They trust Quinkin and hold his hand. 
After that, they slowly make their way to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:42.080
elevator and start it. As the doors close, they&nbsp;
open their eyes and get a glimpse of Quinkin’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:47.280
gruesome face. Thankfully, the doors shut before&nbsp;
he can attack and the kids are brought back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:52.720
their original reality. They see that the framed&nbsp;
picture is upside down and finally sigh of relief.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:57.600
While walking back to the room, Nita asks Max how&nbsp;
she found out that they should close their eyes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:03.120
Max mentions the boiler man and says that he&nbsp;
is blind. Nita stops her and inquires what that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:08.720
means. Then, she notices that Max isn't wearing&nbsp;
her favorite black sandals that she was wearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:13.760
when they first entered the elevator. Max also&nbsp;
mentions their grandmother and claims that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:19.840
is dead. Soon, Nita realizes that they picked up&nbsp;
Max from a different reality who was lost in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:25.040
maze as them. She is not the girl they grew&nbsp;
up with but is from a parallel universe. 
&nbsp;

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:30.000
When they reach their room, the group is beyond&nbsp;
surprised to see that the real Max is already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.640
there. She is trying to explain everything&nbsp;
to her parents who clearly don't believe her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:39.440
That is until they get a look at their&nbsp;
daughter’s doppelganger and freeze in shock.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:43.920
The movie ends as the real Max begs&nbsp;
her parents to keep the other Max&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:47.360
as their fourth daughter. 
